  "style": {
    "name": "Indo-Persian sun-temple of the Meridian Order",
    "rationale": "Second pass: split each flank into TWO stacked half-niches per the document, recessed by exclusion and broken by continuous string-courses every ~8 rows so no field rises flat; deepened the central iwan to a 4-block ogee-arched cavity framed in a gold-and-quartz band with a lapis mihrab inlay at its back; gave the onion dome a belly that overhangs the drum two blocks each side so it never collapses into a pyramid; held the amber↔azure palette exactly (smooth red sandstone body, lapis crown/inlays, sparing gold finials and arch band, quartz pinstripes only) and kept minarets and corner chattris ENGAGED to the single facade plane rather than freestanding."
